    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa98f980_bb58a28b",
        "filename": "keystone/common/cache/_memcache_pool.py",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 708
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-09-17T05:41:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e it\u0027s possible that we have more than _maxsize\n\nNo, its not. We\u0027re leaving previous loop on one of two conditions: either we have connection in pool or we have some quota to create new connections. So if we failed in try: block, then pool is empty and number of connections currently not in the pool is less than maxsize.",
      "parentUuid": "fa98f980_c6b754f4",
      "revId": "db0de93809561fc1f647d4f5c9d53ddd16d18478",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa98f980_8ec54c0c",
        "filename": "keystone/common/cache/_memcache_pool.py",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 81,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-09-17T15:17:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Depending on how eventlet handles a yield (largely dependent on the memcache lib, which we don\u0027t control, today it doesn\u0027t look like we have that issue, but we should be defensive) we could yeild in the ._create_connection step, which would open the door for another coroutine to create a connection between when we do the check and when another thread attempts the creation.\n\nIt is a minor issue which I\u0027ve addressed with an extra try/except in a later patch (minimal over head).",
      "parentUuid": "fa98f980_bb58a28b",
      "revId": "db0de93809561fc1f647d4f5c9d53ddd16d18478",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
